<article class="env-lemma" id="06XG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06XG">Lemma <span data-tag="06XG">96.19.9</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{U} \to \mathcal{X}$ be a $1$-morphism of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let $\tau \in \{ Zar, {\acute{e}tale}, smooth, syntomic, fppf\} $. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is an object of $\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{X}_\tau , \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every object $x$ of $\mathcal{X}$ there exists a covering $\{ x_ i \to x\} $ in $\mathcal{X}_\tau $ such that each $x_ i$ is isomorphic to $f(u_ i)$ for some object $u_ i$ of $\mathcal{U}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the category $\mathcal{U}$ has equalizers, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the functor $f$ is faithful. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there is a first quadrant spectral sequence of $\Gamma (\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$-modules </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_1^{p, q} = H^ q((\mathcal{U}_ p)_\tau , f_ p^*\mathcal{F}) \Rightarrow H^{p + q}(\mathcal{X}_\tau , \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> converging to the cohomology of $\mathcal{F}$ in the $\tau $-topology. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof of this lemma is identical to the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/06XF" data-tag="06XF">96.19.8</a> except that it uses an injective resolution in $\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{X}_\tau , \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$ and it uses Lemma <a href="/tag/06X2" data-tag="06X2">96.17.6</a> instead of Lemma <a href="/tag/06X1" data-tag="06X1">96.17.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>